<title>GERMANY: German electronics industry sees no recovery in 97.</title>
<headline>German electronics industry sees no recovery in 97.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German electronics industry group ZVEI said on Thursday that it did not expect any acceleration of growth in 1997, after a relatively weak 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;We still need to wait for the economic recovery in the German electronics industry,&quot; said Franz-Josef Wissing, ZVEI managing director.</p>
<p>Wissing said sales and output in the industry had risen two percent in the first nine-months of 1996 and domestic output for the full year would probably be more than 226 billion marks ($150.1 billion). ($ = 1.505 German Marks)</p>
